[{"id":2720435211,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6iJowL","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"be81b0685f1e0d588faa9a8d70aca4b81006a718","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce"},"body":"This change seems correct to me. Notably, this also matches `bindings_generator.cpp` behavior.\r\n\r\nAnyone working with internal classes should probably instantiate through the C++ class interface.\r\nThe exception (as @dsnopek noted in the meeting) might be serialization, but we aren't aware of internal classes being serialized in this way.\r\n\r\nI say we merge this early in the dev cycle, and if somebody or something complains, we may need to back paddle. \r\n\r\nSide note, I did search through the code base a bit to find instances of internal classes and make some research, but was surprised to see `GDREGISTER_INTERNAL_CLASS` isn't used once in the code base. So i didn't actually end up finding any.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102440#pullrequestreview-2720435211","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102440","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-03-27T09:09:18Z"},{"id":2722290110,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6iQtm-","state":"DISMISSED","commit_id":"be81b0685f1e0d588faa9a8d70aca4b81006a718","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?u=4a42fd867f2c449fcc23adf635dd574dae98e6c2&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://git